## Question 1: Stack Using an Array

A **stack** follows the **LIFO** (Last In, First Out) rule: the last item pushed is the first item popped. This implementation has a fixed capacity and supports `PUSH`, `POP`, `PEEK`, and `DISPLAY`.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class Stack {
private:
    static const int CAPACITY = 5;
    int items[CAPACITY];
    int topIndex;

public:
    Stack() : topIndex(-1) {}

    bool isEmpty() const {
        return topIndex == -1;
    }

    bool isFull() const {
        return topIndex == CAPACITY - 1;
    }

    void push(int value) {
        if (isFull()) {
            cout << "Stack Overflow: cannot push " << value << ".\n";
            return;
        }

        items[++topIndex] = value;
        cout << value << " pushed onto the stack.\n";
    }

    void pop() {
        if (isEmpty()) {
            cout << "Stack Underflow: cannot pop from an empty stack.\n";
            return;
        }

        cout << items[topIndex--] << " popped from the stack.\n";
    }

    void peek() const {
        if (isEmpty()) {
            cout << "Stack is empty; no top element.\n";
            return;
        }

        cout << "Top element: " << items[topIndex] << '\n';
    }

    void display() const {
        if (isEmpty()) {
            cout << "Stack is empty.\n";
            return;
        }

        cout << "Stack (top to bottom): ";
        for (int i = topIndex; i >= 0; --i) {
            cout << items[i] << ' ';
        }
        cout << '\n';
    }
};

int main() {
    Stack stack;

    stack.push(10);
    stack.push(20);
    stack.push(30);
    stack.display();
    stack.peek();
    stack.pop();
    stack.display();

    return 0;
}
```

### Stack complexity

| Operation | Time complexity | Extra space |
|---|---:|---:|
| `PUSH(x)` | O(1) | O(1) |
| `POP()` | O(1) | O(1) |
| `PEEK()` | O(1) | O(1) |
| `DISPLAY()` | O(n) | O(1) |

The fixed array reserves **O(CAPACITY)** total storage. Each operation uses O(1) auxiliary space; `DISPLAY()` prints elements without creating another collection.

If `PUSH` is called when the stack is full, the program reports **Stack Overflow** and leaves the stack unchanged. If `POP` is called when empty, it reports **Stack Underflow**. `PEEK` on an empty stack reports that no top element exists. Because the array has a fixed capacity, it cannot store additional items once full; a larger array or resizable storage would be needed to increase the capacity.

