## How to compile and run

The code blocks above are separate programs because each has its own `main()` function. Save each block into its own `.cpp` file, for example `stack.cpp` and `circular_queue.cpp`, then compile and run them separately with a C++ compiler:

```bash
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic stack.cpp -o stack
./stack

g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic circular_queue.cpp -o circular_queue
./circular_queue
```

On Windows with MinGW, run the generated programs as `stack.exe` and `circular_queue.exe`.
